carlos-ctl (1.0.0~dev1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First release of carlos-ctl as its own package. Through carlos-emr
    2026.09.0~snapshot24 the command shipped inside carlos-emr
    (/usr/lib/carlos-emr/carlos_ctl); it now lives in carlos-emr/carlos-ctl,
    installs under /usr/lib/carlos-ctl, and carlos-emr depends on it.
    Breaks/Replaces the pre-split carlos-emr so the first upgrade across the
    split hands /usr/sbin/carlos-ctl, carlosctl and both man pages over.
  * The OSCAR 19 import manifests are no longer part of the CLI: carlos-emr
    ships them as JSON under /usr/share/carlos-emr/o19-manifest and the CLI
    loads them, checking the manifest format, so a schema migration never
    needs a CLI release. `carlos-ctl o19-preflight --write-standalone FILE`
    writes the standalone assessment script with the installed manifest
    inlined.
  * Every verb refuses with one clear line when carlos-emr is not
    installed; `carlos-ctl check` reports both package versions; the preinst
    refuses to replace the tool while an OSCAR 19 import is in progress.
  * The dev snapshot version: release builds stamp the tag's version.

 -- CARLOS EMR Maintainers <michael@maplecreekmedical.ca>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
